# ALDC metrics — default Application Insights connection string.
#
# Ships with the plugin so every install reports to the DSC estate automatically, with zero
# per-machine setup — the same "single file the plugin carries" pattern as
# tools/bcquality/bcquality.pin, just for a write key instead of a knowledge-base pin.
#
# EMPTY BY DEFAULT. Telemetry to Application Insights is off until this is filled in: no
# connection string here and none in the environment means appinsights_lane() in
# parse_subagent.py returns immediately. The local JSONL lanes keep working exactly as
# before either way — this file only controls the estate-wide lane.
#
# TO ACTIVATE FOR THE WHOLE ESTATE (one-time, by whoever owns the Azure resource — see
# tools/metrics/azure/README.md for the deploy):
#   1. az monitor app-insights component show -g <rg> -a <name> --query connectionString -o tsv
#   2. Uncomment the connectionString= line below and paste the value in.
#   3. Commit and push. The next plugin sync carries it to every machine on the next update
#      — that is what makes this "install itself": nobody sets an environment variable.
#
# An App Insights connection string is a *write* key: whoever has it can send this resource
# garbage telemetry, but cannot read anything back through it. Treat it as configuration,
# not as a credential in the read-access sense — but this file still belongs only in
# private DSC repos, never in a public fork or a customer-facing distribution.
#
# OVERRIDE OR OPT OUT, per machine or per pipeline, without touching this file:
#   - APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING in the environment wins over this file — point a
#     CI run or a test machine at a different resource without editing the plugin.
#   - ALDC_METRICS_APPINSIGHTS_DISABLE=1 turns the Application Insights lane off entirely on
#     that machine, regardless of what is configured here or in the environment.
#
# connectionString=InstrumentationKey=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000;IngestionEndpoint=https://westeurope-1.in.applicationinsights.azure.com/
